      <div type="clause" n="2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ExcomVII">Excom VII</ref> 2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="Excom VII 2" corresp="#wit-cx"><pb n="438" ed="#liebermann"/>Mid ealdorlicnesse ælmihtiges Godes, þæs fæder ⁊ þæs sunu ⁊ þas halgan gastes, ⁊ eac swylce s<hi rend="italic">anct</hi>a<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ExcomVII_2.lnote.oe.1"/> Marian, ures Drihtenes moder, ⁊ s<hi rend="italic">anct</hi>e Michael<hi rend="italic">is</hi>, þæs halgan heahenglas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ExcomVII_2.lnote.oe.2"/>, ⁊ s<hi rend="italic">anct</hi>us Petrus, þære apostolan alder<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ExcomVII_2.lnote.oe.2"/>, ⁊ þæs halige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ExcomVII_2.lnote.oe.2"/> Nicholaes ⁊ þæs eadigan Augustines ⁊ ealre Chr<hi rend="italic">ist</hi>es halgena,</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="438" ed="#liebermann"/>2. Kraft Ermächtigung des allmächtigen Gottes, des Vaters und des Sohnes und des heiligen Geistes, und ebenso auch sanct<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#ExcomVII_2.lnote.de1.d"/> Marias, unseres Herrn Mutter, und sanct Michaels<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="e" target="#ExcomVII_2.lnote.de1.e"/>, des heiligen Erzengels, und sanct Peters<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="f" target="#ExcomVII_2.lnote.de1.f"/>, der Apostel Fürsten, und des heiligen Nikolaus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="g" target="#ExcomVII_2.lnote.de1.g"/>, und des seligen Augustin [von Canterbury<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="h" target="#ExcomVII_2.lnote.de1.h"/>] und aller<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="f" target="#ExcomVII_2.lnote.de1.f"/> Heiligen Christi,</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">2. By authority of almighty God, the Father and the Son and the Holy Ghost, and likewise also of saint Mary, our Lord’s mother, and of saint Michael, the holy archangel, and of saint Peter, prince of the apostles, and of the holy Nicholas, and of the blessed Augustine [of Canterbury], and of all the saints of Christ,</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text and German translation transcribed from Gesetze I p. 438 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ExcomVII_2.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">438</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sc̄a <hi rend="italic">Hs.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sc̄a MS</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ExcomVII_2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">438</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="ExcomVII_2.lnote.de1.d" n="d" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">438</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> V 1. <hi rend="italic">Die Berufung auf Maria, die Regino noch nicht hat, beweist nicht Abfassung nach</hi> 1066, <hi rend="italic">da in England seit c.</hi> 950 <hi rend="italic">Mariendienst herrscht; vgl. Piper</hi> Kalendarien 50 <hi rend="italic">f.</hi> 94</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. V 1. The invocation of Mary, which Regino does not yet have, does not prove composition after 1066, since in England the cult of Mary has prevailed since c. 950; cf. Piper Kalendarien 50 f. 94</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="ExcomVII_2.lnote.de1.e" n="e" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">438</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> V 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> V 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="ExcomVII_2.lnote.de1.f" n="f" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">438</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> I 11, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> I 11, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="ExcomVII_2.lnote.de1.g" n="g" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">438</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bei Angelsachsen seltener Name (Searle</hi> Onomast. 358); <hi rend="italic">der Cult wird erst nach</hi> 1087 <hi rend="italic">allgemein</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a name rare among the Anglo-Saxons (Searle Onomast. 358); the cult becomes general only after 1087</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="ExcomVII_2.lnote.de1.h" n="h" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">438</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">in Beda’s</hi> Martyrolog. <hi rend="italic">und</hi> Syn. Clovesho. <hi rend="italic">a.</hi> 747, <hi rend="italic">c.</hi> 17</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in Bede’s Martyrolog. and Syn. Clovesho. a. 747, c. 17</seg></note>
      </div>
